   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 09b models\n\nThe **location photo** in group 02 is the background: it is the inpaint canvas, so whatever you\nload there is what the final image is pasted back onto. There is no second background loader.\n\nThe loaders in group 06 are **reference images** (her face, an outfit, a look, or a pose you want\ncopied) \u2014 they steer what gets painted *inside* the mask, they are not backgrounds.\n\n## Models (put them in ComfyUI/models/...)\n\n| File | Folder |\n|---|---|\n| [krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors) | `diffusion_models/` |\n| [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors) | `text_encoders/` |\n| [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_vae.safetensors) | `vae/` |\n| [sdpose_wholebody_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/SDPose/resolve/main/checkpoints/sdpose_wholebody_fp16.safetensors) | `checkpoints/` |\n| [krea2_style_reference.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/loras/krea2_style_reference.safetensors) | `loras/` |\n| [seedvr2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/SeedVR2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/seedvr2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors) | `diffusion_models/` |\n| [seedvr2_ema_vae_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/SeedVR2/resolve/main/vae/seedvr2_ema_vae_fp16.safetensors) | `vae/` |\n| [sigclip_vision_patch14_384.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sigclip_vision_384/resolve/main/sigclip_vision_patch14_384.safetensors) | `clip_vision/` |\n\nYour character LoRA checkpoints go in `models/loras/` (a subfolder per character is fine, e.g. `models/loras/lina/`).\n\nKrea 2 needs a big GPU (RTX 5090 / RTX 6000 Pro class). Run these on RunPod, not a 6 GB card."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1560,
    1450
   ],
   "size": [
    430,
    900
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 19,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 09d Krea 2 - the pose photo's pose, in your location, from a new angle each seed\n\nEach image **starts from the pose photo** (image-to-image, like Workflow 09), so the pose and framing\nare the photo's, and is repainted as your character in your location:\n\n| Input | What it gives |\n|---|---|\n| **Pose photo** (group 07) | the starting image: body pose and framing. *Pose strength* = the sampler's **denoise** |\n| **Picture 1** (group 06) | the person's face and identity (plus the character LoRA in group 01) |\n| **Picture 2** (group 02) | **the room**: walls, furniture, colours, light (a new shot of it, not a copy) |\n| **Picture 3** | the skeleton of the pose, detected on the moved photo |\n\n## Pose strength (sampler denoise, group 04)\n- **0.75**: very close to the pose photo (its colours start to show through too)\n- **0.8**: default - the pose and framing, your person and room\n- **0.9**: only the rough pose\n\n## A new angle per seed (group 05c, *Pose Angle per Seed*)\nBefore encoding, the camera is moved a little around the pose photo: a small turn, tilt, zoom and\nshift, different for every seed. `variation` scales them all (0 = the photo exactly); `max_turn`,\n`max_tilt`, `max_zoom`, `max_shift` set the limits. `candidates` = images per queue, each from its own\nangle. *Pose photo as seen this seed* shows what each candidate starts from.\n\n**Framing (`frame`)**: before the camera moves, the pose photo is cropped around the person to a normal phone shape - by default the location photo's shape when the person fits, otherwise the closest phone shape that does (3:4, 1:1, 4:3, 3:2...). Never padded, so a very wide pose photo can't give a panorama. About 1 MP.\n\n**Folders (`folder_by`)**: every seed of the same prompt is saved in the same folder, `outputs/images/final/9d_<prompt code>/`. Switch to 'queue' for one folder per queue. Background blur and the camera pass run last."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
