   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Several candidates per queue\n\n*Placement & Angle per Seed* (group 05c) turns one queue into **4 candidates** (`candidates`),\neach with its own seed, **its own place** in the location photo and **its own body angle**. No two\ncandidates of a queue share a spot or an angle; the angle is drawn into the skeleton (picture 3)\nand written into the prompt, so the two never disagree.\n\n- `pose` = **new angle per seed**: a fresh standing skeleton per candidate (front, three-quarter,\n  profile, back over the shoulder, to either side), so the pose photo in group 07 is not used.\n  **reference pose**: keep the pose photo's skeleton; it is only moved, rescaled and mirrored.\n- `vary` = **off** restores the old behaviour: same place and pose, only the seed changes.\n- `angles`: the angles to draw from, one per line (`degrees: words for the prompt`; 0 = facing the\n  camera, positive = toward frame-right). Delete the ones you don't want, add your own.\n- `x_min`/`x_max`, `size_min`/`size_max`, `horizon`: the part of the photo she may stand in, how\n  big (near/far), and the photo's eye-level line -- her eyes are put on it.\n- A **painted mask** still wins: every candidate stands where you painted (angle still varies).\n  A **person already in the plate** is replaced in place, the same way.\n\nThey are saved together in `outputs/images/candidates/9b_<seed>/`, each logged with its label.\nHeld for the pod with batch count 10? That's 10 folders. **Workflow 13** picks the winner of a\nfolder into `outputs/images/final/` -- on this PC, no GPU.\n\nEach candidate is a full generation: 4 candidates take 4x as long as 1."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
